{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Two pointers needs sorted data. Sliding window needs contiguity and positive values. When neither holds, the tool that most often rescues an O(N²) solution is a **hash map**."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The operation it gives you"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A hash map answers \"have I seen this value, and if so where?\" in **O(1)** average time — regardless of how many values it holds."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Compare that with searching an array, which is O(N). Swapping an inner search loop for a map lookup is precisely how nested loops collapse into single passes."
    },
